      "text": "Ranch visit and Fiesta Gaucha"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:0a22c0a35cdf7cf4",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "cbd631da1ae1703555d53ad87aa2299aa7debe6b157e6b007dceab3ea4f6bb3f",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-worker-20261107-z3b7r3j6r5-yr8z7okdet",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. You can spend the day at a ranch outside the city.\n\nOn arrival, you’ll be served homemade empanadas. You can then walk around the grounds and go horse riding.\n\nLunch is a traditional Argentine barbecue, or asado. Alcoholic and non-alcoholic drinks, dessert, and coffee or tea are included.\n\nAfter lunch, there’s a show with folk dancing and tango. The gauchos close the show with demonstrations of horsemanship, lasso skills and riding over obstacles.\n\nReturn to Buenos Aires after the show.\n\n**Tour of Buenos Aires and Tigre, Argentina**\n\nOptional\n\n**Tour of Montevideo, the capital of Uruguay**\n\nOptional\n\nThis is a full-day tour.\n\nFerry tickets are included."
    },
